# SpAll — build and dependency artifacts that must never be committed.
#
# The repository is source-only on purpose. `tools/fetch_deps.ps1` re-creates
# third_party/ and `tools/bootstrap_qt.ps1` re-creates .qt/, so neither the ~500 MB of
# dependency sources nor the ~1 GB Qt installation needs to be in git. Keeping them out
# is what makes a clone practical.

# --- build output ------------------------------------------------------------
build/
out/
cmake-build-*/
*.sln
*.vcxproj
*.vcxproj.filters
*.vcxproj.user
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
compile_commands.json

# --- local Qt installation ---------------------------------------------------
.qt/

# --- third-party sources (fetched, not vendored) -----------------------------
third_party/

# --- compiled translation catalogues -----------------------------------------
# The .ts files are the translatable sources and ARE committed; the .qm files are
# build products regenerated by lrelease.
*.qm

# --- runtime / diagnostic output ---------------------------------------------
spall-completion-trace.log
spall-startup-trace.log
spall-selftest-report.txt
*.spv
*.spvasm

# --- editors and tooling -----------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.swp

# --- OS cruft ----------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
